Arthur J. O'Dwyer <ajo@andrew.cmu.edu> deserves a cookie for saying:
> In my most recent game (Reporter-Arc-Hum-Fem-Law) I found myself
> trapped in an owlbear's hug.  So I quaffed a potion of levitation,
> expecting that maybe it might get me out of the hug.  But it didn't.
> In fact (and this I *didn't* expect), I didn't even get a message
> explaining that "the owlbear holds you down!" or anything.
>  Did TDTNTOE in this instance?  Why doesn't levitation interact
> with crushing embraces,

Why should it?  If a kraken can drag you into the water while you're
levitating, why can't an owlbear keep holding you?  Don't think of
levitation like some powerful force.  You know when a balloon loses
just enough pressure that it hovers a few feet off the ground?  Think of
levitation that way, if it helps.

And alternately, even if levitation _is_ powerful and your feet can't be
pulled down to the ground, you're still not very far above the floor
and owlbears are quite big.  

> and with what kinds of things *does* levitation
> interact?
>  I wonder specifically about:

>   Crushing embraces from owlbears, rope golems, and the like;
>   Sticking to mimics and the like;

No interactions, I think.

>   Beartraps - does flying to the ceiling with your leg in a trap
>     do anything good or bad?

The code seems to suggest that you can't float up, since your leg is
still trapped.  Same thing if you're trapped in the floor.

>   If you are levitating and being hugged to death, can you still
>     pick up things from the floor?  If not, does this make sense?

If would assume your body is being pulled upward, making it very
difficult to use gravity or pivot at the waist.  Heck, you shouldn't be
able to grab anything from the floor when you're being hugged anyway.  

Still, it takes a bit of rationalization, as you can see.  ;)  And at
the least, a message would be nice (and trivial to insert).
"You feel your body pulled upward, but you can't escape the owlbear's
embrace!"

